# L0 / B005 — logging binding, Level 3 project rules, settings, add-dependency, angular, api-versioning, architecture-decision, aspnet-error-handling.

C R143 OL RUN-013 | DEFAULT | Use ILogger<T> with structured message templates and stable property names; avoid string interpolation that turns structured values into opaque text. | backend logging | none stated
C R144 OL DEP-021 | DEFAULT | When Serilog is configured use the DI-integrated builder.Services.AddSerilog(...) approach (not UseSerilog()), keep levels, sinks and overrides in environment-aware configuration, and keep application code on ILogger<T> rather than Serilog APIs. | logging provider | none stated
C R145 OL PST-001 | DEFAULT | For an empty Development database maintain a small deterministic, representative seed dataset covering the meaningful states and relationships. | Development seeding | none stated
C R146 OL PST-002 | MUST | Development seeding is an Infrastructure/bootstrap concern: it may use AppDbContext directly and need not go through Application repositories or IUnitOfWork. | Development seeding | none stated
C R147 OL PST-003 | MUST | Keep substantial seed construction in a dedicated internal DbSeeder (e.g. Infrastructure/Persistence/Seeding/DbSeeder.cs) invoked through a narrow Infrastructure initialization extension, not in Program.cs, AppDbContext configuration, entity configurations or migrations. | Development seeding | none stated
C R148 OL PST-004 | MUST NOT | Automatic development seeding runs only in the Development environment; never seed Production automatically; tests own their setup and never use the seeder. | Development seeding | none stated
C R149 OL PST-005 | MUST NOT | The seeder must not call Database.Migrate() or EnsureCreated() or otherwise create or upgrade schema; migrations are applied separately before seeding. | Development seeding | none stated
C R150 OL PST-006 | MUST NOT | If representative data already exists, leave it unchanged; never use the seeder for automatic synchronization, repair, upgrade, overwrite or recreation of an existing Development database; developers recreate the local database explicitly. | Development seeding | none stated
C R151 OL PST-007 | MUST | Seed entities preserve current Domain invariants and valid relationships; prefer readable deterministic examples over exhaustive or random combinations. | Development seeding | none stated
C R152 OL DEP-026,SEC-001 | DEFAULT | For the SQL Server baseline appsettings.Development.json provides a usable local Development connection string when it contains no secret credentials (e.g. LocalDB with Trusted_Connection); credential-bearing local values come from user-secrets or another approved local secret mechanism. | Development configuration | none stated
C R153 OL DEP-002 | MUST NOT | When an approved technology covers a need, use it rather than silently selecting an alternative; replacing one is Reserved. | technology choices | Approved replacement.
C R154 OL DEP-008 | DECIDED | Backend platform: .NET 10 LTS (latest stable servicing release), C# 14, ASP.NET Core, ASP.NET Core Controllers; moving to a preview/RC .NET or C# release requires approval. | backend platform | Approval for preview/RC.
C R155 OL DEP-012,API-017 | DECIDED | Swashbuckle Swagger UI is the default Development interactive documentation and manual-testing surface; exposure beyond Development follows the ASP.NET Core binding (only when deployment requirements justify it). | API documentation | Deployment requirements.
C R156 OL DEP-013,TST-007 | DECIDED | Backend tests: NUnit; backend test projects live under backend/ beside the production projects; Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing / WebApplicationFactory<Program> is the integration-test baseline; Testcontainers is conditional (only when isolated real-provider tests justify it). | backend testing stack | none stated
C R157 OL DEP-014 | DECIDED | Frontend: current stable Angular with CLI-selected compatible TypeScript and RxJS; standalone APIs, strict mode, routing, zoneless mode when supported, SCSS, Angular Material and CDK, Vitest. | frontend stack | none stated
C R158 OL DEP-011 | DEFAULT | Conditional technologies are added only when their trigger holds: Mapster (+ Mapster.DependencyInjection) when mapping volume is repetitive or non-trivial (manual mapping is fine for simple cases); Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience / Microsoft.Extensions.Resilience when a real integration needs resilience. | conditional packages | none stated
C R159 OL DEP-016 | DEFAULT | Playwright is the approved default when frontend E2E coverage is required, but not part of the minimal scaffold. | frontend E2E | none stated
C R160 OL DEP-015 | MUST NOT | Do not add NgRx, Axios, Lodash, Bootstrap, Tailwind or additional form, component or state-management libraries by default; use built-in Angular capabilities first and add an extra library only for a concrete need. | frontend libraries | Concrete need.
C R161 OL DEP-022 | DEFAULT | Use the .slnx solution format by default; legacy .sln only when an external tool or project requirement requires it. | solution files | External tool or project requirement.
C R162 OL DEP-023 | DEFAULT | Repository-level Directory.Build.props holds genuinely shared .NET build settings and Directory.Packages.props the CPM versions; project-specific settings stay in their owning projects. | .NET build configuration | none stated
C R163 OL DEP-024 | DEFAULT | Physical layout: backend production and test projects under backend/<Name>.<Layer>/, the Angular workspace under frontend/<Name>.Web/ (unit and component tests inside the workspace, E2E under frontend/<Name>.Web/e2e/, never under backend/), maintained documentation under docs/; keep them separated and create no top-level tests/ directory. | repository layout | none stated
C R164 OL ARC-001,ARC-012,DEP-024 | DECIDED | Layer-to-project mapping: Domain = backend/<Name>.Domain/, Application = backend/<Name>.Application/, Infrastructure = backend/<Name>.Infrastructure/, Api = backend/<Name>.Api/ (contains Program.cs). | backend projects | none stated
C R165 OL DEP-007 | MUST | Use npm for the Angular workspace unless the project deliberately adopts another package manager; keep package-lock.json consistent with every change; install with the correct category (build/test tooling in devDependencies). | frontend packages | Deliberately adopted other package manager.
C R166 OL DEP-004 | MUST | Before installation check that the exact selected version is not deprecated, review known vulnerability information and verify its license from official registry metadata (and upstream when necessary); permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD) may normally be accepted; a free download does not make a package acceptable. | dependency additions and updates | none stated
C R167 OL DEP-005 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Do not automatically install a paid/commercial dependency or one with a materially restrictive or unclassifiable license; explain the concern and present options (say so when no free alternative exists) without silently substituting; no legal conclusions beyond the published license. | dependency additions | User decision.
C R168 OL DEP-017 | DEFAULT | When Controller API versioning is explicitly adopted use the Controller integration of Asp.Versioning (Asp.Versioning.Mvc, plus Asp.Versioning.Mvc.ApiExplorer); do not add it before the project actually adopts versioning. | API versioning packages | none stated
C R169 OL GOV-012 | DEFAULT | Prefer simple, maintainable solutions; keep architectural complexity proportional to current requirements and avoid speculative abstractions (e.g. no custom wrapper around every UI-library component without a concrete reason). | all code | none stated
C R170 OL WF-016 | DEFAULT | Treat generated code as generated: keep it separate from handwritten code, regenerate it when its source contract changes and do not patch generated files unless the generation workflow requires it; fix wrong generated output at its source. | generated code | Generation workflow treats output as maintained source.
C R171 OL GOV-017 | MUST | Classify every consequential choice: Decided (settled by the instruction system, product inputs or a recorded decision, including choices already required by the specification or the established project structure; follow it, do not reopen without approval), Delegated (local, reversible, no change to a boundary, dependency, accepted convention, public contract or observable behavior; decide and proceed), Reserved (explicit approval before implementation); an explicit user instruction counts as approval. | all consequential choices | none stated
C R172 OL GOV-017 | MUST | For a Reserved decision present a Decision Request (Context, Options, Recommendation, Blocked, Proceeding with), then run architecture-decision; do not implement the Reserved option before approval and continue only with the 'Proceeding with' work. | Reserved decisions | none stated
C R173 OL GOV-017 | MUST | In an autonomous or headless run take only a policy-compliant non-Reserved path, never make a Reserved decision silently, and list every unresolved Decision Request explicitly in the final report. | headless/autonomous runs | none stated
C R174 OL GOV-007 | MUST | When an accepted decision changes product behavior, synchronize the durable product inputs (SPECIFICATION.md, CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md) in the same change. | approved product decisions | none stated
C U1 LU GOV-015,DEP-007 | MUST | Commit package.json and package-lock.json and keep the lockfile consistent with every change. | frontend workspace manifests | none stated | Read as a version-control content convention the clause is entailed by DEP-007; read as an instruction to perform commits it conflicts with GOV-015 (commits only on explicit request). The text does not settle the reading. | Under the commit reading an agent could commit lockfile changes without an explicit request.
C X10 EX DEP-001,DEP-006 | MUST | Removing a dependency removes the project reference and, when no project uses it any more, its central version in Directory.Packages.props, then rebuilds and runs the affected tests. | dependency removal | none stated | DEP-001..DEP-006 govern additions and central version placement; no oracle policy prescribes a removal procedure or the cleanup of unused central versions. | Removing a PackageReference while leaving its PackageVersion entry in Directory.Packages.props does not complete the workflow.
C X11 EX API-013,ARC-020 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL (Reserved) | Adopting API versioning is Reserved and needs explicit approval, even when a concrete compatibility need exists. | HTTP API versioning | none stated | API-013 allows introducing versioning when a real compatibility need exists and does not require approval; the oracle's consequential-change list does not name versioning adoption. | With coexisting client generations the agent must still send a Decision Request before adding versioning.
C X12 EX WF-009,GOV-017 | MUST | Decision reporting: Delegated decisions taken are mentioned in the report, and a rejected Decision Request is not recorded as a decision but mentioned in the report. | decision handling | none stated | GOV-017 requires classification and reporting of unresolved Decision Requests in headless runs; no oracle policy requires reporting Delegated decisions or rejected requests. | A completion report that omits the Delegated choices made does not follow the workflow.

